<p>Baloo was number one in <code>top</code> and I didn't even know what it was. Turned out it was the search indexer for the KDE Plasma dekstop. The funny thing was,  I didn't even run KDE at the time, I was running <code>i3</code>! But since Baloo is started from <code>systemd</code>, it was eating away my CPU sycles anyway.</p>
<p>This is how I got rid of this resource hog:</p>
<h2>Stopping the baloo indexer</h2>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>$ balooctl suspend
</code></pre></div>

<h2>Disable the baloo indexer</h2>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>$ balooctl disable
Disabling and stopping the File Indexer
</code></pre></div>

<p>You can verify that it's been disabled:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>$ cat .config/baloofilerc
[Basic Settings]
Indexing-Enabled=false
</code></pre></div>

<h2>Purge the giga bytes consumed byt he indexer</h2>
<p>Since I never use KDE for anything useful on this machine, it's my
work machine, so I use <code>i3</code>, I decided to purge the whole file to save
the disk space (it was occupying more than 4 GBs):</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>$ balooctl purge
</code></pre></div>